{"id":28184,"slug":"kameradschaft","title":"Kameradschaft","year":1931,"country":"Germany","duration":88,"spine":908,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28184-kameradschaft","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/01f2b09b21d5479965b2b93422ba1072/tUKPob5t1DjOrGRVmJEEfRaalbiOzy_large.jpg","description":"When a coal mine collapses on the frontier between Germany and France and traps a team of French miners, workers on both sides of the border spring into action, putting aside national prejudices and wartime grudges to launch a dangerous rescue operation. Director G. W. Pabst brings a vivid sense of claustrophobia to this ticking-clock scenario, using realistic sets and sound design to create the maze of soot-choked shafts where the miners struggle for survival. Inspired by a real-life mine collapse, Kameradschaft (Comradeship) is an arresting disaster film and a stirring plea for international cooperation, and it cemented Pabst’s status as one of the most morally engaged and formally dexterous filmmakers of his time.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"G. W. Pabst","slug":"g-w-pabst"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Alexander Granach","role":"Kasper","slug":"alexander-granach"},{"actor":"Fritz Kampers","role":"Wilderer","slug":"fritz-kampers"},{"actor":"Daniel Mendaille","role":"Jean Leclerc","slug":"daniel-mendaille"},{"actor":"Ernst Busch","role":"Wittkopp","slug":"ernst-busch"},{"actor":"Elisabeth Wendt","role":"Anna Wittkopp","slug":"elisabeth-wendt"},{"actor":"Gustav Püttjer","role":"Kaplan","slug":"gustav-puttjer"},{"actor":"Oskar Höcker","role":"Mine foreman","slug":"oskar-hocker"},{"actor":"Héléna Manson","role":"Rose, Albert’s wife","slug":"helena-manson"},{"actor":"Andrée Ducret","role":"Françoise Leclerc","slug":"andree-ducret"},{"actor":"Alex Bernard","role":"Grandfather Jacques","slug":"alex-bernard"},{"actor":"Pierre-Louis","role":"Georges, his grandson","slug":"pierre-louis"},{"actor":"Georges Charlia","role":"Emile","slug":"georges